ef "/statistics/medal/country"} "Medals by country"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/medal/athlete"} "Medals by athlete"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/medal_table"} "Medal tables"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/participation"} "Participations"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/records"} "Olympic Records"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/age"} "Age records"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/age_at_death"} "Age at death"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/lists"} "Lists"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/today"} "Today"]] "\n" [:li {}] "\n" [:li {:class "divider"}] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics"} "Statistics"]] "\n"] "\n"] "\n\n\n\n\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/feedbacks/new"} "Feedback"]] "\n" [:form {:class "navbar-form navbar-left", :role "search", :action "/athletes/quick_search", :accept-charset "UTF-8", :method "post"} [:input {:name "utf8", :type "hidden", :value "✓", :autocomplete "off"}] [:input {:type "hidden", :name "authenticity_token", :value "wQ7cJo5aaqg92cD8d4kL3r0QV0zDx4yg4RFu_iT2GVq7x29r87k8Rt9Fdtx9VGTy-xB8rhYx07YFXKo7pEZdoQ", :autocomplete "off"}] [:div {:class "form-group"} "\n" [:input {:type "text", :name "query", :id "query", :class "form-control", :placeholder "Athlete search"}] "\n"] "\n" [:input {:type "submit", :name "commit", :value "Go", :class "btn btn-default", :data-disable-with "Go"}] "\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "container"} "\n" [:ol {:class "breadcrumb"} "\n" [:li {} "\n" [:a {:href "/"} "Home"] "\n"] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/editions"} "Games"]] [:li {} [:a {:href "/editions/7"} "1920 Summer Olympics"]] [:li {} [:a {:href "/editions/7/sports/TOW"} "Tug-Of-War"]] [:li {:class "active"} "Tug-Of-War, Men"] "\n"] "\n" [:div {} [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:span {} "No other events in this sport"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "9009265"} "1870"] "\n" [:option {:value "21100"} "1900"] "\n" [:option {:value "21103"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "926219"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "21115"} "1906"] "\n" [:option {:value "21122"} "1908"] "\n" [:option {:value "21131"} "1912"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/622"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Tug-Of-War, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "17 – 20 August 1920"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/243"} "Olympisch Stadion, Antwerpen"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/21134"} "41 from 5 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament, with a modified Bergvall-type tournament for second-to-fifth place"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "This was the last appearance of the tug-of-war in the Olympics, which made its first appearance at the " [:a {:href "/results/21100"} "1900 Olympics"] ", and was also held in " [:a {:href "/editions/3/sports/TOW"} "1904"] ", " [:a {:href "/results/21115"} "1906"] ", " [:a {:href "/results/21122"} "1908"] ", and " [:a {:href "/results/21131"} "1912"] ". Presumably, the sport was discontinued because of the many controversies that surrounded it. There were several inter-national disputes at the earlier Olympics, but the 1920 Olympic tug-of-war event was conducted without incident."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Great Britain won the tournament easily, winning all six of its pulls. Their team consisted of several former and current members of the London police. Three of the team members, " [:a {:href "/athletes/18034"} "Frederick Humphreys"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/18040"} "Edwin Mills"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/18044"} "James Shepherd"] ", won their third medals and second gold medals. They had been on the silver medal team in 1912 and the gold medal team in 1908. " [:a {:href "/athletes/18043"} "John Sewell"] " also won a second medal, having been on the 1912 runner-up team."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The writing of the " [:strong {} "1920 Official Report"] " was restricted mostly due to the financial problems of the Organizing Committee that occurred after the Games were finished. It resulted in a simple typed report, of which few copies still exist. In addition, the report was not well written and contained many discrepancies, one of these being the results of the tug-of-war competition. Because of this, for a long time, it had been uncertain which team had really won the tug-of-war silver medal during these Olympics, because both the Americans and the Dutch claimed to have won that medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "This may be illustrated by the fact that, in the " [:strong {} "Official Report"] ", the final result of the competition in “Traction á la corde” (Tug-of-war) was:"] "\n\n" [:p {} "1  Grande-Bretagne (Great-Britain)\n2  Hollande (The Netherlands)\n3  Belgique (Belgium)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "The " [:strong {} "Official Report"] " gave a detailed description of the tug-of-war competition, which was held on 17-18 August. The last sentences of that description read:"] "\n\n" [:p {} "“L’Italie déclara forfait devant les Etats-Unis. Les Etats-Unis devaient tirer contre la Hollande pour la seconde place, mais, par suite d’une erreur, l’équipe hollandaise quitta Anvers et ne revint pas pour ce match. Les Etats-Unis se trouveurent de ce fait en seconde place.”"] "\n\n" [:p {} "According to this description, “the Dutch team should have pulled against the American team for second place, but because the Dutch team had already returned home, the second place was then awarded to the United States.”  However, this is incorrect. The Dutch team did complete in the modified Bergvall competition for second place, defeating Belgium two pulls to none. In fact, in the third-place competition, the United States may have left early, and not pulled against Belgium for the bronze medal. It is not certain if the final match took place, but Belgium certainly won the bronze medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "We list nine British athletes, although only eight could pull at a time. We originally included " [:a {:href "/athletes/18050"} "Ernest Thorne"] " and still have him in the results. The great-granddaughter of " [:a {:href "/athletes/18092"} "Alfred Read"] ", however, has contacted us with documentary evidence that her great-grandfather was on the team and won a gold medal, and provided photographs. Thorne is not in the photographs, but it is possible that Read and Thorne pulled in different matches – there are no detailed results for tug-of-war from the 1920 Antwerpen Olympics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Great Britain"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/18024"} "George Canning"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/18032"} "Fred Holmes"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/18034"} "Frederick Humphreys"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/18040"} "Edwin Mills"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/18043"} "John Sewell"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/18044"} "James Shepherd"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/18047"} "Harry Stiff"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/18050"} "Ernest Thorne"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/18092"} "Alfred Read"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Netherlands"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws